:: StoryTitle
Vacancy — A Shenmi Fusu Fan Game

:: StoryData
{"ifid": "B38D22B8-237B-49C0-9861-C2C3D7E21017", "format": "Harlowe", "format-version": "3.3.9", "start": "Vacancy"}

:: Vacancy
(set: $rot to 0, $bell to false, $book to false, $foil to false, $name to false, $saved to false, $looked to false)
<div class="eyebrow">PARANORMAL INCIDENT / CASE 017</div>
<div class="hero"><div class="sigil">017</div><div class="hero-copy"><h1>VACANCY</h1><p>A Shenmi Fusu fan-fiction game</p></div></div>
<div class="quote">The god does not answer prayers.<br>It is checking who still owes it a name.</div>
You are a temporary investigator, barely an hour into the night shift. At 2:17 a.m., a shrine scheduled for demolition appears where the subway exit should be.

The phones of the people who went inside are still ringing. Whenever someone picks up, the same voice answers.

[[Take the shift that should never have been yours->Street]]
<div class="meta">About 5–10 minutes · Five endings · Click choices to continue<br>Contains supernatural horror, death, and loss of identity.<br>No jump scares, sudden audio, or timed choices.<br>Use ↶ to undo a choice. You can restart after any ending.</div>
<div class="credit">Inspired by Shenmi Fusu by Fo Qian Xian Hua. This unofficial fan work features an original cast and incident.</div>

:: Street
<div class="eyebrow">01 / ARRIVAL</div><h2>A street with no way out</h2>
You turn around. The subway entrance is a brick wall. Figures in the windows lower their heads in unison, as though waiting for you to make the first move.

Your colleague's last message remains on your screen:
<blockquote>Ordinary methods cannot kill a ghost. Find its rules before you try to contain it. You can use that borrowed Ghost Eye twice tonight. Open it a third time, and whatever wakes up may no longer be you.</blockquote>
A delivery courier kneels outside the shrine. He keeps repeating, “I already gave you my name. Why won't you let me leave?”

You sigh. Looks like tonight you have to pick a fight with a god.

[[Approach the courier->Threshold]]

:: Threshold
<div class="eyebrow">02 / THE FIRST RULE</div><h2>Do not answer</h2>
From behind the door, your mother's voice calls your full name.

The courier catches your trouser leg. “Don't answer. Ever since I did, it keeps telling me to come inside.”

A red thread around his wrist disappears through the door. Faint words are carved into the threshold: <em>Those who answer shall be entered.</em>

[[Hold your breath. Stay silent->Hall]]
[[Answer “I'm here” to find out if it is your mother->Answer]]

:: Answer
<div class="eyebrow">A RULE HAS BEEN TRIGGERED</div><h2>It heard you</h2>
The voice stops. Your name appears on the door, its final stroke still bleeding ink.

It did not recognize you. You confirmed who you were.

[[Force the Ghost Eye open to sever the new thread (+1 Corruption)->Sever]]
[[Follow your mother's voice inside->Succession]]

:: Sever
(set: $rot to $rot + 1)
<h2>Borrowed sight</h2>
The thing beneath your forehead opens. You see a thread connecting your name to the darkness beyond the door. Your gaze cuts it before it can pull tight.

Something warm runs down your cheek. Your name fades from the wood. Your mother's voice becomes the scraping of timber.

[[Retreat into the hall with the courier->Hall]]

:: Hall
<div class="eyebrow">03 / INVESTIGATION</div><h2>The shrine is empty</h2>
There is no statue on the altar. Only a chair facing the wall. Its back is engraved: <em>The named shall sit. The nameless may return.</em>

The courier sits against a wall. The red thread still bites into his wrist. He no longer dares to look at the chair.

There is no countdown here. Take the time you need to investigate.
<div class="status">(if: $bell)[✓ Bell rule　](if: $book)[✓ Ledger rule　](if: $name)[✓ True name　](if: $foil)[✓ Gold case]</div>
[[Examine the bronze bell->Bell]]
[[Read the offering ledger->Ledger]]
[[Search the altar drawer->Drawer]]
[[Inspect the marks on the chair->Chair]]
[[Deal with the thread around the courier's wrist->Rescue]]
[[Enter the inner sanctuary when you are ready->Sanctuary]]

:: Bell
(set: $bell to true)
<h2>When the bell rings, it seeks a seat</h2>
You gently tap the little bell. The chair turns half an inch toward you. When the sound fades, it stops.

An old label on the bell reads:
<blockquote>One ring invites the god. Two rings seat it.<br>The god knows the names in the ledger, not their faces.</blockquote>
You should not ring it a second time without a plan. You draw back your hand.

[[Remember the rule and return to the hall->Hall]]

:: Ledger
(set: $book to true)
<h2>This is not a book of wishes</h2>
There are names on every page. Beside each, the column marked “Blessing” records a date and a cause of death.

The final page holds the courier's name: <strong>Lin Zhao</strong>. The rest is blank.

A crossed-out note is still legible:
<blockquote>The unnamed are beyond its jurisdiction. Erase a name from the ledger to release its owner.<br>If the god's own name were entered in the offerings column...</blockquote>
Blood obscures the rest. A dish of opaque gold paint sits on the altar, enough to cover the writing.

[[Remember the rule and return to the hall->Hall]]

:: Drawer
(set: $foil to true)
<h2>The previous investigator</h2>
Inside the drawer is a case made from thin sheets of gold, just large enough for the ledger. Its clasp is intact. Fingernail scratches mark its edges.

A note lies inside:
<blockquote>Gold blocks supernatural influence.<br>Sealing the book alone does nothing. The entity is still in the chair.<br>Get it into the book first. Then close the case.</blockquote>
You take the case. It is a containment device, not a weapon.

[[Return to the hall->Hall]]

:: Chair
<h2>A name scraped away</h2>
The back of the chair has been sanded again and again, but pale dust remains in the grooves. Nearby lie a stack of thin ritual paper and a piece of charcoal.

(if: $name)[You already know the name buried here: the Incense Receiver.]
[[Carefully make a charcoal rubbing->Rubbing]]
(if: not $looked)[[[Use the Ghost Eye to see through the wood (+1 Corruption)->Gaze]]]
[[Leave it for now and return to the hall->Hall]]

:: Rubbing
(set: $name to true)
<h2>The Incense Receiver</h2>
Charcoal slowly reveals the inscription: <strong>the Incense Receiver</strong>.

Beneath it, smaller characters read: <em>At first there was no god. The people called it by this name.</em>

You understand. The “god” is a ghost given an identity through worship. Perhaps that same identity can make it obey.

[[Keep the rubbing and return to the hall->Hall]]

:: Gaze
(set: $rot to $rot + 1, $looked to true)
(if: $rot >= 3)[(go-to: "Awakening")]
(else:)[(set: $name to true)
<h2>It is looking back</h2>
The wood turns transparent. Behind it is a silhouette layered with human faces. Every mouth speaks the same name: <strong>the Incense Receiver</strong>.

You close the Eye. Your shadow on the wall takes a moment longer.

You have the name. It cost you more than a sheet of paper would have.
[[Return to the hall->Hall]]]

:: Rescue
<h2>The other end of the thread</h2>
(if: $saved)[Lin Zhao is free. He grips his work badge, checking over and over that his name is still there.
[[Return to the hall->Hall]]]
(else:)[“You didn't come here to pray, did you?” the courier whispers. “Then could you take me with you when you leave?”

(if: $book)[[[Cover “Lin Zhao” in the ledger with gold paint->Erase]]]
[[Suppress the thread with the Ghost Eye (+1 Corruption)->Intervene]]
[[Investigate the rules first and return to the hall->Hall]]]

:: Erase
(set: $saved to true)
<h2>Take away its target</h2>
You do not touch the thread. You simply paint over the name “Lin Zhao.”

It drops to the floor like an ordinary piece of old cotton. Lin Zhao stands up.

“So you don't have to be stronger than it,” he says.

[[Return to the hall->Hall]]

:: Intervene
(set: $rot to $rot + 1)
(if: $rot >= 3)[(go-to: "Awakening")]
(else:)[(set: $saved to true)
<h2>Your blood for his name</h2>
The thread snaps under the Eye's gaze. “Lin Zhao” fades from the ledger, while your shadow stretches an inch closer to the chair.

Lin Zhao steadies you. “You look like you need to get out more than I do.”

[[Return to the hall->Hall]]]

:: Sanctuary
<div class="eyebrow">04 / CONFRONTATION</div><h2>Sigh. I guess it's time to fight a god.</h2>
You carry the ledger and bell into the inner sanctuary. The chair never passed through the doorway, yet it is already waiting in the middle of the room.

A voice from the empty seat says, “Sit down. You can bring them back.”

Outside, a whole street of phones is ringing. Each once belonged to someone who came here for help.

Breaking the chair will not destroy the ghost. But perhaps you can make sure it never rules here as a god again.

[[Return to the hall and keep investigating->Hall]]
[[Open the Ghost Eye and shatter the throne (+1 Corruption)->Attack]]
[[Sit down and take its place->Succession]]
[[Look for a way out while it waits->Escape]]
(if: $bell and $book and $name and $foil)[[[Write “the Incense Receiver” in the offerings column->Trap]]]
(else:)[<div class="hint">Your containment plan is incomplete. You need the bell's rule, the ledger's rule, the god's name, and the gold case.</div>]

:: Attack
(set: $rot to $rot + 1)
(if: $rot >= 3)[(go-to: "Awakening")]
(else:)[<div class="eyebrow">ENDING 01 / FALSE VICTORY</div><h2>You killed a chair</h2>
The wood splits. The ringing stops. The shrine door opens onto the street again.

You step outside. Every shop has its lights on.

Behind every counter stands a chair facing the wall.

<div class="quote">You broke its seat.<br>Now it has a seat everywhere.</div>
<div class="hint">Clue: destroying a vessel does not destroy its ghost. Find a rule that will draw it into the ledger.</div>
[[Start over->Vacancy]]]

:: Succession
<div class="eyebrow">ENDING 02 / THE NEW GOD</div><h2>Someone finally takes over</h2>
As you sit, every prayer in the city pours into your ears. Someone asks for safety. Someone asks for a reunion. Someone only asks not to dream tonight.

You want to help them.

But your hand has already written the first name in the ledger.

<div class="quote">The position has been vacant for a long time.<br>It was never waiting for a hero. Just the next person on the night shift.</div>
<div class="hint">Clue: inheriting the throne means inheriting its killing rules.</div>
[[Start over->Vacancy]]

:: Escape
<div class="eyebrow">ENDING 03 / SURVIVOR</div><h2>Clocking out</h2>
You follow the wall where no names are written. The ghost does not pursue you. It can only claim those who answered and were entered in its ledger.

(if: $saved)[Lin Zhao follows you out. At dawn, he buys you a cup of hot soy milk from a convenience store. Neither of you mentions the night.]
(else:)[Behind you, the courier asks, “Where's the exit?” You do not turn around. Wind swallows the rest of his words.]

Your phone vibrates again. Another emergency call. The same street.

<div class="quote">Survival is an ending.<br>But it is not the end of this incident.</div>
[[Start over->Vacancy]]

:: Trap
<h2>Make the god an offering</h2>
You write “the Incense Receiver” in the offerings column and place the ledger in the open gold case.

The first ring. The chair turns toward the altar.

The second ring. The impression of a seated figure slowly presses into the pages. For the first time, the entity is the target named by its own rule.

Now you must make the final choice.

[[Close the gold case immediately->Containment]]
[[Take one last look inside the book (+1 Corruption)->Last Look]]

:: Last Look
(set: $rot to $rot + 1)
(if: $rot >= 3)[(go-to: "Awakening")]
(else:)[<h2>Do not hold its gaze</h2>
The figure on the page raises its head. It has your face. For a moment, at least.

You slam the case shut. The gold closes, cutting off the voice inside.
[[Confirm containment->Containment]]]

:: Containment
<div class="eyebrow">ENDING 04 / VACANCY</div><h2>You did not kill the ghost.<br>You ended its reign as a god.</h2>
The chair is an ordinary old chair again. Names disappear from the door, one by one. The phones in the street fall silent.

(if: $saved)[Lin Zhao helps you lift the heavy case. “Come on,” he says. “Your shift is over.”]
(else:)[The red thread falls from the courier's wrist. Lin Zhao stumbles after you. “Wait for me. I'm clocking out too.”]

After sunrise, the case is transferred to containment storage. Number 017. In the notes, you write: <em>Do not open. Do not worship.</em>

(if: $rot is 0)[You never used the Ghost Eye. Your most effective weapon was reading the rules to the end.]
(else:)[The Eye beneath your forehead has not gone back to sleep. It reminds you that every use has a price.]

<div class="quote">On the day the shrine was demolished, nobody knelt.</div>
[[Play again and try different choices->Vacancy]]

:: Awakening
<div class="eyebrow">ENDING 05 / THE GHOST AWAKENS</div><h2>The third time, it is not you who opens the Eye</h2>
You try to close it. Your body does not obey.

You can see the street, the shrine, and the person lying on the ground. They are wearing your clothes. Their phone still displays a warning they never finished reading.

<div class="quote">A new line is added to the incident report:<br>A second supernatural entity is now present at the scene.</div>
<div class="hint">Clue: the third use of the Ghost Eye always causes a takeover. Reading, making a rubbing, and erasing a name cost no Corruption.</div>
[[Start over->Vacancy]]

:: Status [header]
(if: (passage:)'s name is not "Vacancy")[<div class="hud"><span>CASE 017 · VACANCY</span><span>GHOST EYE · CORRUPTION (print: $rot) / 3</span></div>]

